{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>You shall not make a cut for the dead.</b> Such is the way of the Emorites — to scratch their flesh when a dead person dies among them." "<b>And you shall not place a tattoo.</b> A writing that is etched and sunk in, never erased, for he pricks it with a needle and it remains black forever." "<b>Tattoo.</b> From the root of ״וְהוֹקַע אוֹתָם״ (Numbers 25) and ״וְהוֹקַעְנוּם״ (II Samuel 21) — they drive a piece of wood into the ground and hang them on it; thus the letters are found pressed in and driven into the ground; פורפו״ינט בְּלַעַ״ז."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {2 "the la'az is Old French porfoint, 'pierced through / driven deep'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:18.570760689Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}